---
// Privacy policy. Text copied verbatim from the SharedCue/index.html policy page
// (last updated 8 September 2026) — keep the two in sync if either changes.
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="SharedCue Privacy Policy"
			description="What SharedCue collects, what never leaves your phone, and what you can do about it."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
			}
			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 0.2em;
				font-size: 2.2em;
			}
			.updated {
				margin-top: 0;
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
			}
			h2 {
				margin: 1.6em 0 0.4em;
				font-size: 1.35em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>SharedCue Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="updated">Last updated: 8 September 2026</p>

			<p>
				SharedCue ("we", "us") is a shared checklist app. It is built to hold as little of your
				information as it can. This policy explains exactly what reaches our servers, what never
				leaves your phone, and what you can do about it.
			</p>

			<h2>What we collect</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Your phone number, stored only as a one-way hash.</strong> You sign in with your mobile
					number and a one-time code. Our server keeps a hash of that number, not the number itself, so
					it can recognise you when you sign in again.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>An account identifier.</strong> We assign your account an ID, and register a key and
					push token for each device you use, so your devices can sync with each other and receive
					notifications.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Your lists, encrypted.</strong> Your groups, categories and items sync between you and
					the people you share them with. They are end-to-end encrypted: they pass through our server,
					but we cannot read them.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>What never leaves your phone</h2>
			<p>
				Your address book is never uploaded. When SharedCue shows a group member by the name you saved
				for them, that matching happens entirely on your device. We also do not collect your location,
				photos, or payment details.
			</p>

			<h2>What we do not do</h2>
			<p>
				SharedCue contains no analytics, advertising or crash-reporting services of any kind. We do not
				track you across other companies' apps or websites, we do not show ads, and we do not build
				profiles about you.
			</p>

			<h2>How we use what we hold</h2>
			<p>
				Only to run the app: signing you in, syncing your lists to the people you share them with, and
				sending reminders and notifications you have asked for.
			</p>

			<h2>Sharing</h2>
			<p>
				Content you put in a shared list is visible to the other members of that list — that is the
				point of the app. Beyond that, we share data only with the service providers who run our
				infrastructure, and where the law requires it.
			</p>

			<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
			<p>
				We keep your account while you use it. You can ask us to delete it by emailing the address below;
				when you do, your account record and the encrypted data associated with it are removed within 30
				days, apart from backups that expire on their own shortly after. Data stored on your own device is
				removed when you delete the app.
			</p>

			<h2>Security</h2>
			<p>
				Your lists are encrypted end-to-end in transit and encrypted at rest on your device. No service
				can promise perfect security, but the design deliberately limits what we could disclose even if
				we were compelled to.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				SharedCue is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their
				information.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask us for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
				it. Write to the address below and we will respond within a reasonable time.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes materially, we will update the date above and, where appropriate, notify
				you in the app.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
